@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Certificate slice: three two-place obstruction cores
+
+Status: **UNSEALED SKELETON**.  The terminal seal marker is deliberately
+absent until all replay and negative controls pass.
+
+## Scope, frozen inputs, and conventions
+
+## Executive result
+
+| kill | terminal unit / residues | minimal slice | deepest `t` | outer coefficients | bridge rows | verdict |
+|---|---|---:|---:|---|---|---|
+| `(99,66), delta=2` | `stage4_J_d159_k35 = 6264` | pending | pending | pending | pending | pending |
+| `(99,66), delta=5/2` | `stage8_G_local16_coord0 = 64` | pending | pending | pending | pending | pending |
+| `D=108, delta=3` | `r71=-2*j2`, `r81=2*j1^2`, `r80=-c-j1^4+9*j1*j2^2` | pending | pending | pending | pending | pending |
+
+## 1. Provenance model and recursive slice rule
+
+## 2. Kill A: `(99,66), delta=2`
+
+### 2.1 Back-substitution DAG and zero-facts
+
+### 2.2 Minimal certificate of `1`
+
+### 2.3 Replay and perturbation control
+
+## 3. Kill B: `(99,66), delta=5/2`
+
+### 3.1 Back-substitution DAG and zero-facts
+
+### 3.2 Minimal localized certificate of `1`
+
+### 3.3 Replay and perturbation control
+
+## 4. Kill C: `D=108, delta=3`
+
+### 4.1 Common-`h3` expansion through local power 8
+
+### 4.2 Thirteen labels, seven Jacobian pivots, and the three residues
+
+### 4.3 Minimal localized certificate of `1`
+
+### 4.4 Replay and perturbation control
+
+## 5. One filtered obstruction map
+
+### 5.1 Incidence block, first-point Jacobian bands, and filtration
+
