   303	a linear system on the nine-or-fewer coordinates `B1c_{n-1,q}` whose lowest `w`-power
   304	is exactly **35** — which is why `J`-band coordinates `k<35` are vacuous and the
   305	charged prefix rows `k=17..26` and stage-0 row `k=27` reduce to `0=0`. Its rank is
   306	full except where the outer `D1` offset-0 rows (weight 93, 8 rows on 8 columns,
   307	invertible) have already zeroed a column: they hit `B1c_{3,21}` and `B1c_{7,18}`,
   308	which is precisely why the joint sequence reads `9,9,9,8,8,8,8,7` rather than
   309	`9,9,9,9,8,8,8,8`. The branch asymmetry has an equally concrete source
   310	(`pole_row_triviality.py`): the `F` pole rows are identically zero throughout, and
   311	the `G` pole rows are nonzero at `delta=2` local powers `5,6,7,8` (every stage from
   312	1) but at `delta=5/2` only at *even* local powers `10,12,14,16` (every second
   313	stage, because `t=s^2`). `delta=2` therefore collides with the `J` band four stages
   314	earlier. That is the whole of the four-stage gap between the two deaths.
