   316	## 8. Controls (all in my engine)
   317	
   318	**8.1 Zero-point / end-to-end (`C2`).** Set every free chart coordinate to zero, so
   319	`F=P^9`, `G=P^6` and `J(F,G) == 0` identically. My **unfactored** four-term `KJ`
   320	is identically zero on every `(t,w)` slot, and `KF`'s top form is exactly
   321	`w^27 (w-1)^72 = P^9`. `PASS`.
   322	
   323	**8.2 Tame automorphism (`C1`).** Requested: degrees `>= 6`, two-point. I must
   324	report a premise problem: by the classical Jung-van der Kulk structure theorem, for
   325	a plane polynomial automorphism with `max(deg) > 1` the leading forms `in F` and
   326	`in G` are powers of a **common** linear form, so the pair
   327	has **one** point at infinity; a genuine two-point configuration of degrees `>= 6`
   328	with `J=1` would be a Keller pair that is not an automorphism, i.e. the object whose
   329	non-existence is under test. So `NOT-APPLICABLE[TWO-POINT, deg>=6]`, and the
   330	charged design's own two-point control is at degrees `(1,1)` for the same reason.
   331	I therefore built the strongest available substitute — a **tame automorphism of
   332	degrees 6 and 36** whose single point at infinity lies inside my chart:
   333	
   334	```text
   335	F = x + y^6,     G = y + (x + y^6)^6,     J(F,G) = 1  (verified directly),
   336	in F = y^6,      in G = y^36,             point at infinity  w = y/x = 0.
   337	```
   338	
   339	Running it through my generic normalized Jacobian for degrees `(n,m)=(6,36)`, the
   340	entire band family collapses: `KJ` has exactly one nonzero slot,
   341	`[t^{n+m-2} w^0] = [t^40 w^0] = 1`, and **every** other `(t,w)` slot vanishes. Since
   342	the rows my engine imposes on `(99,66)` are precisely such slots, the machinery does
   343	not falsely kill this automorphism. `SURVIVES[ALL JACOBIAN BANDS I CAN RUN]`.
   344	`NOT-APPLICABLE[s=3 tower, outer D1/D2, minor split; degrees (6,36) have no such
   345	configuration]`.
   346	
   347	**8.3 Discriminating power (`C1b`).** Perturbing one homogeneity weight
   348	(`n -> n-1`) in the Jacobian makes the same automorphism control **fail**
   349	(8 violated slots). The control is not vacuous.
   350	
   351	**8.4 Relaxation controls (`C3`,`C4`) — what actually kills `delta=2`.**
   352	Re-running `delta=2` with the Jacobian band dropped: **survives** stage 4 at
   353	dimension 945, no residue. Re-running with the pole rows dropped: **survives** at
   354	915, no residue. Neither family alone is inconsistent; the death is exactly their
   355	interaction. This rules out the failure mode "the setup is inconsistent, so
   356	everything dies".
   357	
   358	**8.5 Pivot-order convention (`C5`).** Re-ran both branches under plain
   359	lexicographic symbol-name order (the charged engine's stated order) instead of my
   360	inert-first preference: identical dimension paths and identical residues
   361	`6264` and `64`.
   362	
   363	**8.6 Cost of the one imported convention (`C6`).** Dropping `Hc_11_0=0` raises every
   364	`delta=5/2` dimension by exactly 1 (`6703,1064,1017,975,941,914,895,881,870`) and
   365	leaves the stage-8 residue at exactly `64`. The imported Xu-ODE input is
   366	dimension-only.
   367	
   368	**8.7 Moh p.208 `(64,48) -> (16,12)` — `GAP`, disclosed.** I extracted printed
   369	pp. 207–209 from the frozen PDF. The prose reads ("... the total number of
