   652	sequence.  Purely numeric factors refute this universal determinant, and a
   653	killed control invalidates it.  Stop after three covered clients if no stable
   654	support or factor survives.
   655	
   656	**Information gain:** very high: one bounded extraction separates a theorem
   657	from three unrelated successful computations.
   658	
   659	### Card 3 — coverage-first chart atlas and honest survivor recomposition
   660	
   661	**Label/dependencies:** `NEW CONNECTION`; Moh/Xu order modules, split
   662	classification, explicit gauge actions, exact localization, and typed descent.
   663	It does not assume the provisional `(25,15)` kill.
   664	
   665	**Mechanism/claim:** emit the full source module, chart module, explicit map,
   666	and one machine-checked containment label:
   667	
   668	```text
   669	COVERING_ISOMORPHISM, COVERING_RELAXATION, RESTRICTED_SLICE, or OPEN_MAP.
   670	```
   671	
   672	Only the first two license a kill.  Towers carry a triangular inverse and
   673	omitted monomials become named cokernel coordinates.  Any covered survivor is
   674	recomposed to full `F,G`, with every omitted term restored and the Jacobian
   675	checked coefficientwise over characteristic zero.
   676	
   677	**Cheapest test/bound:** on `(25,15)`, construct the orbit map from the full
   678	envelope to its five tower parameters/seven lower `h` monomials for all three
   679	partitions and report cokernel rank.  One lane-hour; no standard basis unless
   680	the map covers.
   681	
   682	**Outcomes/stop:** cokernel zero lets the existing unit ideals finish the row;
   683	positive cokernel identifies the smallest enlarged chart.  A covered survivor
   684	is the strongest honest counterexample lead.  Do not run all 166 groups before
   685	one positive coverage control; stop any `RESTRICTED_SLICE` whose complement is
   686	uncovered.
   687	
   688	**Information gain:** high: it hardens kills and creates a legitimate
   689	counterexample pipeline.
   690	
   691	## 8. Single first lane
   692	
   693	**Launch `two-place-obstruction-core-sol56` as the first new lane after the
   694	four current gates seal.**  Do not launch another fixed-`t` cone computation.
   695	
   696	Objective: from the exact, source-covered portions of `(99,66)`, the `D=108`
   697	split chart, and `(25,15)`, back-substitute every unit/Q-star pivot and emit a
   698	minimal certificate of `1` whose rows retain provenance
   699	`{incidence,outer,pole,Jacobian,localization}`.  Express the three cores as
   700	minors or Schur complements of one filtered obstruction map and attempt to
   701	replace numerical skeleton entries by the symbols `(d_s,u_s,V_s,delta)`.
   702	Include a tame-automorphism negative control and refuse `(25,15)` as theorem
   703	input unless its running gate supplies a covering map.
   704	
   705	Bound: 90 minutes reasoning, three desk computations each `<10 min` and
   706	`<4 GB`, no new standard basis, no fleet.  Deliver either (i) a stable
   707	tree-indexed support/minor rule and the next symbolic lemma, (ii) a
   708	filtration-page rule with different first pages, or (iii) `NO_PATTERN` with
   709	the precise substituted constants that prevent generalization.  Stop at
   710	`NO_PATTERN` after the third client.  This lane has the highest information
   711	gain because it decides whether the campaign has found a theorem mechanism or
   712	only a successful finite engine.
   713	
   714	## 9. Running-lane dispositions (receipts only)
